WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.000
FilmSub.lk — සිංහල උපසිරැසි සමඟ (Auto Sinhala Subtitles)

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:26.110
Does Ser Hugh have any family in the capital?

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:27.770
No.

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:31.810
I stood vigil for him myself last night.

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.830
He had no one else.

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:38.740
He'd never worn this armor before.

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:42.790
Bad luck for him - going against the Mountain.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.130
Who determines the draw?

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:47.370
All the knights draw straws, Lord Stark.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:49.290
Aye.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.630
But who holds the straws?

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:55.890
You've done good work, Sisters.

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:02.550
Life is strange.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:06.100
Not so many years ago we fought as enemies at the Trident.

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:09.140
I'm glad we never met on the field, Ser Barristan.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:12.480
As is my wife. I don't think the widow's life would suit her.

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:14.820
You're too modest.

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:17.450
I've seen you cut down a dozen great knights.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:21.110
My father once told me you were the best he'd ever seen.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:24.170
I never knew the man to be wrong about matters of combat.

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:26.460
He was a fine man, your father.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:29.500
What the Mad King did to him was a terrible crime.

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:33.340
And that lad - he was a squire until a few months ago.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:36.470
How could he afford a new suit of armor?

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:38.960
Perhaps Lord Arryn left him some money?

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:44.400
- I hear the king wants to joust today. - Yes, that will never happen.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:47.230
Robert tends to do what he wants.

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:49.850
If the king got what he wanted all the time,

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:52.520
he'd still be fighting a damned rebellion.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:00.530
It's made too small, Your Grace. It won't go.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:03.370
Your mother was a dumb whore with a fat arse.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.540
Did you know that?

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:11.040
Look at this idiot! One ball and no brains.

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:13.960
He can't even put a man's armor on him properly.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:16.970
- You're too fat for your armor. - Fat?

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:19.510
Fat, is it?

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:22.060
Is that how you speak to your king?

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:31.070
It's funny, is it?

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:36.030
- No, Your Grace. - No?

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:38.520
You don't like the Hand's joke?

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:40.910
You're torturing the poor boy.

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:43.700
You heard the Hand. The king's too fat for his armor.

00:04:43.870 --> 00:04:46.790
Go find the breastplate stretcher - now!

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:52.080
"The breastplate stretcher"?

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:54.330
How long before he figures it out?

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:57.580
- Maybe you should have one invented. - All right, all right.

00:04:57.760 --> 00:05:00.680
You watch me out there. I still know how to point a lance.

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:03.420
You've no business jousting. Leave that for the young men.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:06.900
Why, because I'm king? Piss on that. I want to hit somebody!

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:09.150
- And who's going to hit you back? - Anybody who can.

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:12.150
- And the last man in his saddle... - Will be you.

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:16.690
There's not a man in the Seven Kingdoms would risk hurting you.

00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:19.120
Are you telling me those cowards would let me win?

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:20.950
Aye.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:28.740
- Drink. - I'm not thirsty.

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:31.240
Drink. Your king commands it.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:37.000
Gods,

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.630
too fat for my armor.

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:43.130
Your squire - a Lannister boy?

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:45.720
A bloody idiot,

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:47.850
but Cersei insisted.

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:51.310
I have Jon Arryn to thank for her.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:54.320
"Cersei Lannister will make a good match," he told me.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:57.150
"You'll need her father on your side."

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:03.120
I thought being king meant I could do whatever I wanted.

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:08.200
Enough of this. Let's go watch 'em ride.

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:11.000
At least I can smell someone else's blood.

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.160
- Robert. - What?

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:19.540
An inspiring sight for the people, eh?

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:22.540
Come, bow before your king! Bow, you shits!

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:39.570
- Where's Arya? - At her dancing lessons.

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:45.070
The Knight of the Flowers.

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:53.160
Thank you, Ser Loras.

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:26.900
Don't let Ser Gregor hurt him.

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:29.700
- Hey. - I can't watch.

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:34.750
A hundred gold dragons on the Mountain.

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:38.580
- I'll take that bet. - Now what will I buy with 100 gold dragons?

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:40.710
A dozen barrels of Dornish wine?

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:43.890
Or a girl from the pleasure houses of Lys?

00:07:44.050 --> 00:07:47.890
- Or you could even buy a friend. - He's going to die.

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:49.880
Ser Loras rides well.

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:22.130
Such a shame, Littlefinger.

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:25.460
It would have been so nice for you to have a friend.

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:27.460
And tell me, Lord Renly,

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:29.960
when will you be having your friend?

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:44.230
Loras knew his mare was in heat. Quite crafty, really.

00:08:44.900 --> 00:08:46.610
Ser Loras would never do that.

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:50.700
- There's no honor in tricks. - No honor and quite a bit of gold.

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:54.920
Sword!

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:22.570
Leave him be!

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:46.710
Stop this madness in the name of your king!

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.920
Let him go!

00:10:03.690 --> 00:10:05.570
I owe you my life, ser.

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:07.900
I'm no ser.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:33.040
Remove his hood.

00:10:33.220 --> 00:10:36.270
On that eve, the captive Imp

00:10:36.430 --> 00:10:39.940
Downwards from his horse did limp

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:43.110
No more would he preen and primp

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:44.860
In garb of red and gold

00:10:45.020 --> 00:10:46.560
This isn't the Kingsroad.

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:50.520
- You said we were riding for Winterfell. - I did... Often and loudly.

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:56.320
Very wise. They'll be out in droves, looking for me in the wrong place.

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:59.400
Word's probably gotten to my father by now.

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:02.040
He'll be offering a handsome reward.

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:05.290
Everyone knows a Lannister always pays his debts.

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:07.800
Would you be so good as to untie me?

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:11.210
- And why would I do that? - Why not?

00:11:11.380 --> 00:11:14.710
Am I going to run? The hill tribes would kill me for my boots.

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:16.420
Unless a shadowcat ate me first.

00:11:16.590 --> 00:11:19.550
Shadowcats and hill tribes are the least of your concerns.

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:24.270
The eastern road.

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:26.310
We're going to the Vale.

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:30.110
You're taking me to your sister's to answer for my imagined crimes.

00:11:30.270 --> 00:11:34.190
Tell me, Lady Stark, when was the last time you saw your sister?

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:36.980
- Five years ago. - She's changed.

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:41.660
She was always a bit touched, but now... You might as well kill me here.

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:44.960
- I am not a murderer, Lannister. - Neither am I.

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:47.410
I had nothing to do with the attempt on your son's life.

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:49.330
- The dagger found... - What sort of imbecile

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:51.160
arms an assassin with his own blade?

00:11:51.340 --> 00:11:53.390
- Should I gag him? - Why?

00:11:53.550 --> 00:11:55.390
Am I starting to make sense?

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:58.350
Rodrik!

00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:03.850
My lady, this way.

00:12:20.620 --> 00:12:22.370
Untie me.

00:12:22.530 --> 00:12:25.450
If I die, what's the point?

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:19.130
- Rodrik? - I'll be fine, my lady.

00:13:19.930 --> 00:13:22.270
There's no need to bloody yourself.

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:25.590
Your first?

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:28.760
You need a woman.

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:31.100
Nothing like a woman after a fight.

00:13:33.230 --> 00:13:35.140
I'm willing if she is.

00:13:47.830 --> 00:13:49.630
Bran.

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:53.450
The Iron Islands. Sigil - a kraken.

00:13:53.630 --> 00:13:55.670
Words - "We do not sow."

00:13:55.840 --> 00:13:57.930
- Lords? - The Greyjoys.

00:13:58.090 --> 00:14:01.390
Famed for their skills at archery, navigation and lovemaking.

00:14:03.220 --> 00:14:05.310
And failed rebellions.

00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:11.640
Sigil - a stag, a crowned stag now that Robert's king.

00:14:11.810 --> 00:14:14.770
- Good. - Words - "Ours is the fury."

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:17.490
Lords - the Baratheons.

00:14:17.650 --> 00:14:19.490
The Westerlands.

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:21.650
Sigil - a lion.

00:14:21.820 --> 00:14:24.820
- Words - "A Lannister always pays his debts." - No.

00:14:25.450 --> 00:14:28.330
A common saying, but not their official motto.

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:30.450
Lords - the Lannisters.

00:14:30.620 --> 00:14:33.450
- We're still on their words. - I don't know them.

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:35.500
You do know them. Think.

00:14:35.670 --> 00:14:38.090
"Unbowed, unbent, unbroken."

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:40.830
- That's House Martell. - "Righteous in wrath."

00:14:41.010 --> 00:14:44.470
- House Hornwood. - "Family, duty, honor."

00:14:44.640 --> 00:14:46.520
Those are Tully words - your mother's.

00:14:46.680 --> 00:14:50.190
- Are we playing a game? - Family, duty, honor...

00:14:50.350 --> 00:14:52.520
- Is that the right order? - You know it is.

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:54.680
Family comes first?

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:58.980
Your mother had to leave Winterfell to protect the family.

00:14:59.150 --> 00:15:01.570
How can she protect the family

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:04.030
if she's not with her family?

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:07.370
Your mother sat by your bed

00:15:07.530 --> 00:15:10.200
for three weeks while you slept.

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:12.460
And then she left!

00:15:14.210 --> 00:15:17.210
When you were born, I was the one who pulled you from your mother.

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:21.250
I placed you in her arms.

00:15:21.420 --> 00:15:25.210
From that moment until the moment she dies,

00:15:26.220 --> 00:15:28.730
she will love you.

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:30.560
Absolutely.

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:34.680
- Fiercely. - Why did she leave?

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:36.640
I still can't tell you,

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:39.230
- but she will be home soon. - Do you know where she is now?

00:15:39.400 --> 00:15:40.950
Today?

00:15:41.110 --> 00:15:43.740
- No, I don't. - Then how can you promise me

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:45.900
she'll be home soon?

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:51.320
Sometimes I worry you're too smart for your own good.

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:54.920
I'll never shoot another arrow.

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:58.330
And where is that written?

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:01.040
You need legs to work a bow.

00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:03.670
If the saddle Lord Tyrion designed actually works,

00:16:03.840 --> 00:16:06.220
you could learn to shoot a bow from horseback.

00:16:06.380 --> 00:16:08.090
Really?

00:16:09.090 --> 00:16:11.630
Dothraki boys learn when they're four years old.

00:16:11.810 --> 00:16:13.810
Why shouldn't you?

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:30.940
Keep it down.

00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:33.540
You're not supposed to be inside the castle walls.

00:16:33.700 --> 00:16:36.910
I thought you were supposed to be an important person around here.

00:16:37.080 --> 00:16:39.330
Important enough for the likes of you.

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:42.750
You're not the only nobleman in my life, you know.

00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:46.290
Who, the Imp? I'd call him half a nobleman.

00:16:46.470 --> 00:16:48.350
Jealous?

00:16:48.510 --> 00:16:50.220
Why should I be jealous?

00:16:50.390 --> 00:16:53.310
Anyone with a few coppers in his pocket can own you for the night.

00:16:54.140 --> 00:16:56.480
What's a dwarf like down below?

00:16:56.640 --> 00:16:58.680
I've always wondered.

00:16:58.850 --> 00:17:01.890
Might surprise you.

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:06.150
He's good with his fingers too. And his tongue.

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:09.160
Generous tipper.

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:11.990
I guess gold is cheap for a Lannister.

00:17:12.160 --> 00:17:14.000
You are jealous.

00:17:14.160 --> 00:17:18.000
I'm a Greyjoy. We've been lords of the Iron Islands for 300 years.

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:20.910
There's not a family in Westeros that can look down on us,

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:22.950
not even the Lannisters.

00:17:23.130 --> 00:17:25.130
And what about the Starks?

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:29.290
I've been Lord Stark's ward since I was eight years old.

00:17:29.470 --> 00:17:32.850
A ward - that's a nice word for it.

00:17:33.010 --> 00:17:35.800
Your father rebelled against King Robert and if he does it again...

00:17:35.970 --> 00:17:39.100
My father fought for the freedom of his people.

00:17:39.270 --> 00:17:42.860
What did your father do? Fucked a cook and whelped a whore.

00:17:43.020 --> 00:17:45.480
You're a very serious boy.

00:17:45.650 --> 00:17:48.820
- I'm not a boy. - Yes, you are.

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:53.780
A serious boy with a serious cock.

00:17:53.950 --> 00:17:56.210
I don't want to pay for it.

00:17:56.370 --> 00:17:59.040
Then get yourself a wife.

00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:04.550
Come on.

00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:08.170
I'm not gonna hurt you.

00:18:15.390 --> 00:18:17.850
How is your son, my lord?

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:20.720
He'll never walk again.

00:18:22.690 --> 00:18:24.690
But his mind is sound?

00:18:25.560 --> 00:18:27.600
So they say.

00:18:27.770 --> 00:18:29.900
A blessing, then.

00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:34.190
I suffered an early mutilation myself.

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:38.570
Some doors close forever...

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:42.870
others open in most unexpected places.

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:45.750
May I?

00:18:50.340 --> 00:18:53.220
If the wrong ears heard what I'm about to tell you,

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:55.420
off comes my head.

00:18:55.590 --> 00:18:58.130
And who would mourn poor Varys then?

00:18:58.310 --> 00:19:01.940
North or South, they sing no songs for spiders.

00:19:02.940 --> 00:19:04.400
But there are things you must know.

00:19:04.560 --> 00:19:07.890
You are the King's Hand and the king is a fool -

00:19:08.070 --> 00:19:12.780
your friend, I know, but a fool - and doomed unless you save him.

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:15.450
I've been in the capital a month.

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:19.330
Why have you waited so long to tell me this?

00:19:19.490 --> 00:19:21.200
I didn't trust you.

00:19:21.370 --> 00:19:23.700
So why do you trust me now?

00:19:24.620 --> 00:19:28.580
The queen is not the only one who has been watching you closely.

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:30.830
There are few men of honor in the capital.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:32.670
You are one of them.

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:36.710
I would like to believe I am another, strange as that may seem.

00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:39.430
What sort of doom does the king face?

00:19:39.600 --> 00:19:42.310
The same sort as Jon Arryn.

00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:46.360
The tears of lys, they call it.

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:48.770
A rare and costly thing,

00:19:48.940 --> 00:19:52.450
as clear and tasteless as water. It leaves no trace.

00:20:01.790 --> 00:20:03.500
Who gave it to him?

00:20:03.660 --> 00:20:06.660
Some dear friend, no doubt. But which one?

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:11.040
There were many. Lord Arryn was a kind and trusting man.

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:13.290
There was one boy.

00:20:13.460 --> 00:20:15.960
All he was he owed to Jon Arryn.

00:20:17.050 --> 00:20:19.050
The squire, Ser Hugh?

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:23.050
Pity, what happened to him,

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:26.350
just when his life seemed to be going so nicely.

00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:30.560
If Ser Hugh poisoned him...

00:20:31.820 --> 00:20:34.070
who paid Ser Hugh?

00:20:35.070 --> 00:20:39.540
- Someone who could afford it. - Jon was a man of peace.

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:43.170
He was Hand for 17 years - 17 good years.

00:20:43.330 --> 00:20:45.130
Why kill him?

00:20:46.040 --> 00:20:49.380
He started asking questions.

00:21:17.950 --> 00:21:20.700
He's found one bastard already.

00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:24.950
He has the book. The rest will come.

00:21:25.120 --> 00:21:27.420
And when he knows the truth, what will he do?

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:29.250
The gods alone know.

00:21:29.410 --> 00:21:32.370
The fools tried to kill his son.

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:35.210
What's worse - they botched it.

00:21:37.710 --> 00:21:40.460
The wolf and the lion will be at each other's throats.

00:21:41.220 --> 00:21:44.270
- We will be at war soon, my friend. - What good is war now?

00:21:44.430 --> 00:21:46.440
We're not ready.

00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:49.110
If one Hand can die, why not a second?

00:21:49.270 --> 00:21:51.820
This Hand is not the other.

00:21:51.980 --> 00:21:53.530
We need time.

00:21:53.690 --> 00:21:56.780
Khal Drogo will not make his move until his son is born.

00:21:56.940 --> 00:22:00.230
- You know what these savages are. - "Delay", you say.

00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:02.320
"Move fast", I reply.

00:22:02.490 --> 00:22:05.750
This is no longer a game for two players.

00:22:05.910 --> 00:22:07.920
It never was.

00:22:27.180 --> 00:22:30.510
The first to arrive and the last to leave.

00:22:31.940 --> 00:22:34.110
I admire your industry.

00:22:34.270 --> 00:22:36.850
You do move quietly.

00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:39.480
We all have our qualities.

00:22:40.780 --> 00:22:42.530
You look a bit lonely today.

00:22:42.700 --> 00:22:44.950
You should pay a visit to my brothel this evening.

00:22:45.120 --> 00:22:47.540
- First boy is on the house. - I think you're mistaking

00:22:47.700 --> 00:22:50.570
- business with pleasure. - Am I?

00:22:52.330 --> 00:22:56.330
All those birds that whisper in your ear - such pretty little things.

00:22:57.840 --> 00:22:59.930
Trust me,

00:23:00.460 --> 00:23:02.670
we accommodate all inclinations.

00:23:03.680 --> 00:23:07.770
I'm sure. Lord Redwyne likes his boys very young, I hear.

00:23:07.930 --> 00:23:12.680
I'm a purveyor of beauty and discretion - both equally important.

00:23:12.850 --> 00:23:17.430
Though I suppose beauty is a subjective quality, no?

00:23:17.610 --> 00:23:22.030
Is it true that Ser Marlon of Tumblestone prefers amputees?

00:23:22.190 --> 00:23:24.860
All desires are valid to a man with a full purse.

00:23:25.030 --> 00:23:28.360
And I heard the most awful rumor about a certain lord

00:23:28.530 --> 00:23:30.530
with a taste for fresh cadavers.

00:23:31.330 --> 00:23:34.840
Must be enormously difficult to accommodate that inclination.

00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:36.880
The logistics alone...

00:23:37.040 --> 00:23:40.210
to find beautiful corpses before they rot.

00:23:40.380 --> 00:23:44.430
Strictly speaking, such a thing would not be in accordance with the king's laws.

00:23:44.590 --> 00:23:47.010
Strictly speaking.

00:23:49.970 --> 00:23:54.720
Tell me. Does someone somewhere keep your balls in a little box?

00:23:56.230 --> 00:23:58.240
I've often wondered.

00:23:59.730 --> 00:24:01.390
Do you know, I have no idea where they are.

00:24:01.570 --> 00:24:05.240
And we had been so close.

00:24:05.400 --> 00:24:09.240
But enough about me. How have you been since we last saw each other?

00:24:09.410 --> 00:24:11.920
Since you last saw me or since I last saw you?

00:24:12.080 --> 00:24:15.380
Now the last time I saw you, you were talking to the Hand of the King.

00:24:15.540 --> 00:24:18.260
- Saw me with your own eyes? - Eyes I own.

00:24:18.420 --> 00:24:19.920
Council business.

00:24:20.090 --> 00:24:23.050
We all have so much to discuss with Ned Stark.

00:24:23.210 --> 00:24:28.170
Everyone's well aware of your enduring fondness for Lord Stark's wife.

00:24:29.260 --> 00:24:32.630
If the Lannisters were behind the attempt on the Stark boy's life

00:24:32.810 --> 00:24:38.110
and it was discovered that you helped the Starks come to that conclusion...

00:24:38.270 --> 00:24:41.230
to think a simple word to the queen...

00:24:41.400 --> 00:24:43.610
One shudders at the thought.

00:24:43.780 --> 00:24:46.200
But you know something? I do believe that I have seen you

00:24:46.360 --> 00:24:48.230
even more recently than you have seen me.

00:24:48.410 --> 00:24:51.120
- Have you? - Yes.

00:24:51.280 --> 00:24:55.450
Earlier today, I distinctly recall seeing you talking to Lord Stark in his chambers.

00:24:55.620 --> 00:24:57.700
Was that you under the bed?

00:24:57.870 --> 00:24:59.740
And not long after that

00:24:59.920 --> 00:25:02.550
when I saw you escorting a certain

00:25:03.210 --> 00:25:05.670
foreign dignitary...

00:25:05.840 --> 00:25:08.180
Council business?

00:25:08.340 --> 00:25:11.470
Of course, you would have friends from across the Narrow Sea.

00:25:11.640 --> 00:25:14.190
You're from there yourself, after all.

00:25:14.350 --> 00:25:17.440
We're friends, aren't we, Lord Varys?

00:25:17.890 --> 00:25:19.760
I'd like to think we are.

00:25:19.940 --> 00:25:22.110
So you can imagine my burden,

00:25:22.270 --> 00:25:25.850
wondering if the king might question my friend's sympathies.

00:25:26.030 --> 00:25:29.950
To stand at a crossroads where turning left means loyalty to a friend,

00:25:30.110 --> 00:25:31.860
turning right loyalty to the realm...

00:25:32.030 --> 00:25:34.320
- Please. - To find myself in a position

00:25:34.490 --> 00:25:36.360
where a simple word to the king...

00:25:36.540 --> 00:25:38.630
What are you two conspiring about?

00:25:39.710 --> 00:25:42.010
Well, whatever it is, you'd best hurry up.

00:25:42.170 --> 00:25:45.180
- My brother is coming. - To a small council meeting?

00:25:45.340 --> 00:25:48.220
Disturbing news from far away.

00:25:49.840 --> 00:25:51.840
Hadn't you heard?

00:26:20.960 --> 00:26:22.840
Off with you. No begging.

00:26:23.000 --> 00:26:24.830
I'm not a beggar. I live here.

00:26:25.000 --> 00:26:27.080
D'you want a smack on your ear to help you with your hearing?

00:26:27.250 --> 00:26:29.040
I want to see my father.

00:26:29.210 --> 00:26:31.880
I want to fuck the queen, for all the good it does me.

00:26:32.050 --> 00:26:33.710
You want your father, boy?

00:26:33.890 --> 00:26:37.940
He's lying on the floor of some tavern, getting pissed on by his friends.

00:26:38.100 --> 00:26:40.520
My father is Hand of the King!

00:26:40.680 --> 00:26:43.140
I'm not a boy. I'm Arya Stark of Winterfell.

00:26:43.310 --> 00:26:46.640
And if you lay a hand on me, my father will have both your heads on spikes.

00:26:46.820 --> 00:26:49.740
Now are you going to let me by or do I need to smack you

00:26:49.900 --> 00:26:52.400
on the ear to help with your hearing?

00:26:54.030 --> 00:26:57.030
You know I had half my guard out searching for you?

00:27:00.370 --> 00:27:03.700
- You promised me this would stop. - They said they were going to kill you.

00:27:03.870 --> 00:27:06.500
- Who did? - I didn't see them,

00:27:06.670 --> 00:27:08.430
- but I think one was fat. - Arya.

00:27:08.590 --> 00:27:11.140
I'm not lying! They said you found the bastard

00:27:11.300 --> 00:27:14.140
and the wolves are fighting the lions and the savage...

00:27:14.300 --> 00:27:15.960
Something about the savage.

00:27:16.140 --> 00:27:18.440
- Where did you hear this? - In the dungeons,

00:27:18.600 --> 00:27:21.770
- near the dragon skulls. - What were you doing in the dungeons?

00:27:23.310 --> 00:27:24.970
Chasing a cat.

00:27:27.610 --> 00:27:28.780
Pardon, my lord.

00:27:28.940 --> 00:27:32.190
There's a night's watchman here begging a word. Says it's urgent.

00:27:39.450 --> 00:27:42.120
- Your name, friend? - Yoren, if it please.

00:27:43.410 --> 00:27:46.240
- This must be your son. He has the look. - I'm a girl!

00:27:46.420 --> 00:27:47.960
Did Benjen send you?

00:27:48.130 --> 00:27:52.090
No one sent me, my lord. I'm here to find men for the Wall,

00:27:52.260 --> 00:27:55.760
see if there's any scum in the dungeons that might be fit for service.

00:27:55.930 --> 00:27:58.520
- We'll find recruits for you. - Thank you, my lord.

00:27:58.680 --> 00:28:00.980
But that's not why I disturb you now.

00:28:02.310 --> 00:28:05.070
Your brother Benjen, his blood runs black -

00:28:05.230 --> 00:28:07.440
makes him as much my brother as yours.

00:28:08.480 --> 00:28:12.770
It's for his sake I rode here so hard I damn near killed my horse.

00:28:12.940 --> 00:28:14.770
There are others riding too.

00:28:15.030 --> 00:28:17.160
The whole city will know by tomorrow.

00:28:17.320 --> 00:28:19.650
Know what?

00:28:19.830 --> 00:28:22.330
Best said in private, my lord.

00:28:28.040 --> 00:28:31.000
Go on. We'll talk more later.

00:28:31.670 --> 00:28:34.040
Jory, take her safely to her room.

00:28:34.210 --> 00:28:36.670
Come along, my lady. You heard your father.

00:28:42.760 --> 00:28:47.390
- How many guards does my father have? - Here in King's Landing? Fifty.

00:28:47.560 --> 00:28:50.100
You wouldn't let anyone kill him, would you?

00:28:50.270 --> 00:28:52.980
No fear on that count, little lady.

00:28:57.740 --> 00:29:01.080
- Well? - It's about your wife, my lord.

00:29:02.990 --> 00:29:05.200
She's taken the Imp.

00:29:21.350 --> 00:29:23.230
You're far from home, Lady Stark.

00:29:23.390 --> 00:29:27.900
- To whom do I speak? - Ser Vardis Egan, knight of the Vale.

00:29:28.060 --> 00:29:32.140
- Is Lady Arryn expecting your visit? - There was no time to send word.

00:29:32.310 --> 00:29:34.440
May I ask, my lady,

00:29:34.610 --> 00:29:36.360
why he is with you?

00:29:36.530 --> 00:29:39.120
That's why there was no time.

00:29:39.280 --> 00:29:41.910
- He is my prisoner. - He doesn't look like a prisoner.

00:29:42.070 --> 00:29:45.240
My sister will decide what he looks like.

00:29:45.910 --> 00:29:49.030
Yes, my lady. She will at that.

00:29:55.090 --> 00:29:58.470
The Eyrie. They say it's impregnable.

00:29:59.760 --> 00:30:02.180
Give me ten good men and some climbing spikes,

00:30:02.340 --> 00:30:04.550
I'll impregnate the bitch.

00:30:05.390 --> 00:30:07.400
I like you.

00:30:17.230 --> 00:30:19.190
Lord Stark, your presence has been requested

00:30:19.360 --> 00:30:21.610
in the small council chamber. A meeting has been called.

00:30:21.780 --> 00:30:23.820
I need to see the king first - alone.

00:30:23.990 --> 00:30:26.200
The king is at the small council meeting, my lord.

00:30:26.370 --> 00:30:28.290
He has summoned you.

00:30:28.450 --> 00:30:31.280
- Is it about my wife? - No, my lord.

00:30:31.460 --> 00:30:34.090
I believe it concerns Daenerys Targaryen.

00:30:34.250 --> 00:30:38.460
- The whore is pregnant. - You're speaking of murdering a child.

00:30:38.630 --> 00:30:41.000
I warned you this would happen, back in the North.

00:30:41.180 --> 00:30:43.720
I warned you, but you didn't care to hear.

00:30:43.890 --> 00:30:46.140
Well, hear it now.

00:30:47.140 --> 00:30:49.650
I want 'em dead, mother and child both.

00:30:49.810 --> 00:30:51.820
And that fool Viserys as well.

00:30:51.980 --> 00:30:55.320
Is that plain enough for you? I want them both dead.

00:30:55.480 --> 00:30:57.980
You will dishonor yourself forever if you do this.

00:30:58.150 --> 00:31:01.650
Honor?! I've got seven kingdoms to rule!

00:31:01.820 --> 00:31:04.860
One king, seven kingdoms.

00:31:05.030 --> 00:31:07.240
Do you think honor keeps them in line?

00:31:07.410 --> 00:31:09.460
Do you think it's honor that's keeping the peace?

00:31:09.620 --> 00:31:13.950
- It's fear - fear and blood. - Then we're no better than the Mad King.

00:31:14.120 --> 00:31:18.330
- Careful, Ned. Careful now. - You want to assassinate a girl

00:31:18.500 --> 00:31:20.040
because the spider heard a rumor?

00:31:20.210 --> 00:31:22.920
No rumor, my lord. The princess is with child.

00:31:23.090 --> 00:31:26.340
- Based on whose information? - Ser Jorah Mormont.

00:31:26.510 --> 00:31:28.680
He is serving as advisor to the Targaryens.

00:31:28.850 --> 00:31:31.230
Mormont? You bring us the whispers

00:31:31.390 --> 00:31:34.890
of a traitor half a world away and call it fact?

00:31:35.060 --> 00:31:37.680
Jorah Mormont's a slaver, not a traitor.

00:31:37.860 --> 00:31:40.200
Small difference, I know, to an honorable man.

00:31:40.360 --> 00:31:43.950
He broke the law, betrayed his family, fled our land.

00:31:44.110 --> 00:31:49.820
- We commit murder on the word of this man? - And if he's right? If she has a son?

00:31:49.990 --> 00:31:53.240
A Targaryen at the head of a Dothraki army -

00:31:53.410 --> 00:31:57.200
- what then? - The Narrow Sea still lies between us.

00:31:57.380 --> 00:32:01.430
I'll fear the Dothraki the day they teach their horses to run on water.

00:32:01.590 --> 00:32:03.470
Do nothing?

00:32:03.630 --> 00:32:05.880
That's your wise advice?

00:32:06.050 --> 00:32:09.550
Do nothing till our enemies are on our shores?

00:32:09.720 --> 00:32:11.760
You're my council. Counsel!

00:32:11.930 --> 00:32:15.560
Speak sense to this honorable fool.

00:32:15.730 --> 00:32:19.570
I understand your misgivings, my lord.

00:32:19.730 --> 00:32:22.270
Truly, I do. It is a terrible thing

00:32:22.440 --> 00:32:24.400
we must consider, a vile thing.

00:32:24.570 --> 00:32:26.730
Yet we who presume to rule

00:32:26.910 --> 00:32:28.910
must sometimes do vile things

00:32:29.070 --> 00:32:31.240
for the good of the realm.

00:32:31.410 --> 00:32:34.700
Should the gods grant Daenerys a son,

00:32:34.870 --> 00:32:38.660
- the realm will bleed. - I bear this girl no ill will,

00:32:38.830 --> 00:32:42.580
but should the Dothraki invade, how many innocents will die?

00:32:42.750 --> 00:32:45.040
How many towns will burn?

00:32:45.220 --> 00:32:48.430
Is it not wiser, kinder even,

00:32:48.590 --> 00:32:53.720
that she should die now so that tens of thousands might live?

00:32:53.890 --> 00:32:56.430
We should have had them both killed years ago.

00:32:56.600 --> 00:32:58.770
When you find yourself in bed with an ugly woman,

00:32:58.940 --> 00:33:02.150
best close your eyes, get it over with.

00:33:02.320 --> 00:33:05.410
Cut her throat. Be done with it.

00:33:11.870 --> 00:33:14.460
I followed you into war -

00:33:14.620 --> 00:33:16.580
twice,

00:33:16.750 --> 00:33:18.500
without doubts,

00:33:18.670 --> 00:33:20.670
without second thoughts.

00:33:21.420 --> 00:33:23.590
But I will not follow you now.

00:33:24.510 --> 00:33:26.550
The Robert I grew up with

00:33:26.720 --> 00:33:30.140
didn't tremble at the shadow of an unborn child.

00:33:32.180 --> 00:33:34.020
She dies.

00:33:35.470 --> 00:33:37.300
I will have no part in it.

00:33:37.480 --> 00:33:39.650
You're the King's Hand, Lord Stark.

00:33:39.810 --> 00:33:43.270
You'll do as I command or I'll find me a Hand who will.

00:33:52.200 --> 00:33:54.410
And good luck to him.

00:33:54.580 --> 00:33:58.290
- I thought you were a better man. - Out. Out, damn you.

00:33:58.460 --> 00:34:00.170
I'm done with you.

00:34:01.290 --> 00:34:04.250
Go, run back to Winterfell!

00:34:04.420 --> 00:34:06.760
I'll have your head on a spike!

00:34:08.170 --> 00:34:11.000
I'll put it there myself, you fool!

00:34:11.180 --> 00:34:16.100
You think you're too good for this? Too proud and honorable? This is a war!

00:34:19.020 --> 00:34:22.030
I'll go ahead with my daughters. Get them ready. Do it yourself.

00:34:22.190 --> 00:34:24.950
- Don't ask anyone for help. - Right away, my lord.

00:34:25.110 --> 00:34:27.660
Lord Baelish is here for you.

00:34:28.990 --> 00:34:31.280
His Grace went on about you at some length

00:34:31.450 --> 00:34:35.290
after you took your leave. The word "treason" was mentioned.

00:34:36.830 --> 00:34:40.130
- What can I do for you? - When do you return to Winterfell?

00:34:40.290 --> 00:34:43.130
- Why? What do you care? - If you're still here come nightfall,

00:34:43.290 --> 00:34:46.920
I'll take you to see the last person Jon Arryn spoke with before falling ill.

00:34:47.090 --> 00:34:49.550
If that sort of thing still interests you.

00:34:50.550 --> 00:34:52.220
I don't have the time.

00:34:52.380 --> 00:34:55.420
It won't take more than an hour. But as you please.

00:35:00.850 --> 00:35:04.060
Round up all the men we have and station them outside the girls' chambers.

00:35:04.940 --> 00:35:07.610
- Who are your best two swords? - Heward and Wyl.

00:35:07.770 --> 00:35:10.900
Find them and meet me at the stables.

00:35:15.740 --> 00:35:18.320
You bring him here without permission?

00:35:18.950 --> 00:35:21.240
You pollute my home with his presence?

00:35:24.330 --> 00:35:28.670
Your aunt has done a bad thing, Robin, a very bad thing.

00:35:28.840 --> 00:35:30.720
You remember her, don't you?

00:35:31.920 --> 00:35:33.670
Isn't he beautiful?

00:35:33.840 --> 00:35:36.800
And strong too. Jon knew it.

00:35:36.970 --> 00:35:39.760
His last words were "The seed is strong."

00:35:39.930 --> 00:35:42.350
He wanted everyone to know what a good, strong boy

00:35:42.520 --> 00:35:44.980
his son would grow up to be.

00:35:45.150 --> 00:35:48.240
Look at him, the lord of all the Vale.

00:35:48.400 --> 00:35:50.610
Lysa,

00:35:50.780 --> 00:35:53.120
you wrote me about the Lannisters,

00:35:53.280 --> 00:35:56.240
- warning me... - To stay away from them!

00:35:56.410 --> 00:35:58.960
Not to bring one here!

00:35:59.120 --> 00:36:01.330
Mummy...

00:36:01.500 --> 00:36:04.500
- is that the bad man? - It is.

00:36:06.670 --> 00:36:08.920
He's little.

00:36:09.090 --> 00:36:11.180
He's Tyrion the Imp, of House Lannister.

00:36:12.510 --> 00:36:15.220
He killed your father. He murdered the Hand of the King!

00:36:15.380 --> 00:36:17.800
Did I kill him too?

00:36:17.970 --> 00:36:22.090
- I've been a very busy man. - You will watch your tongue!

00:36:23.100 --> 00:36:24.970
These men are knights of the Vale.

00:36:25.140 --> 00:36:29.770
Every one of them loved Jon Arryn. Every one of them would die for me.

00:36:29.940 --> 00:36:33.310
If any harm comes to me, my brother Jaime will see that they do.

00:36:33.490 --> 00:36:36.330
You can't hurt us. No one can hurt us here. Tell him, Mummy!

00:36:36.490 --> 00:36:40.290
- Tell him! - My sweet boy.

00:36:40.830 --> 00:36:44.840
He's just trying to frighten us. Lannisters are all liars.

00:36:45.540 --> 00:36:47.630
No one will hurt my baby.

00:36:47.790 --> 00:36:49.450
Mummy...

00:36:50.340 --> 00:36:53.010
I want to see the bad man fly.

00:36:55.090 --> 00:36:58.420
- Perhaps you will, my little love. - This man is my prisoner.

00:36:59.140 --> 00:37:01.980
I will not have him harmed.

00:37:03.430 --> 00:37:05.100
Ser Vardis,

00:37:05.680 --> 00:37:07.970
my sister's guest is weary.

00:37:08.600 --> 00:37:10.680
Take him down below so he can rest.

00:37:11.690 --> 00:37:13.690
Introduce him to Mord.

00:37:16.320 --> 00:37:18.570
You go sleep, dwarf man.

00:37:18.740 --> 00:37:20.790
Sleep good, little dwarf man!

00:37:56.570 --> 00:37:58.910
Lord Stark's lucky he still has a head.

00:37:59.070 --> 00:38:01.650
Robert will rant for a few days, but he won't do anything.

00:38:01.820 --> 00:38:04.910
- He adores the man. - You're jealous.

00:38:05.990 --> 00:38:08.620
- Are you sure this won't hurt? - Only if I slip.

00:38:12.750 --> 00:38:16.000
And you'd prefer me like this?

00:38:16.170 --> 00:38:18.590
If you want hairless, maybe you should find a little boy.

00:38:18.760 --> 00:38:20.760
I want you.

00:38:21.800 --> 00:38:24.880
My brother thinks that anyone who hasn't been to war isn't a man.

00:38:25.060 --> 00:38:27.480
He treats me as if I'm a spoilt child.

00:38:29.100 --> 00:38:30.760
And you're not?

00:38:31.730 --> 00:38:33.940
Loras Tyrell, the Knight of the Flowers?

00:38:34.110 --> 00:38:36.240
How many wars have you fought in?

00:38:36.400 --> 00:38:39.610
And how much did your father spend on that armor of yours?

00:38:39.780 --> 00:38:41.620
Hold still.

00:38:42.780 --> 00:38:45.610
All I ever hear from Robert and Stannis is how I'm not tough enough,

00:38:45.780 --> 00:38:47.490
how I squirm at the sight of blood.

00:38:47.660 --> 00:38:50.240
You did vomit when that boy's eye was knocked out in the melee.

00:38:50.410 --> 00:38:52.290
His eye was dangling out of the damn socket!

00:38:52.460 --> 00:38:55.010
He shouldn't have entered the melee if he didn't know how to fight.

00:38:55.170 --> 00:38:58.300
Easy for you to say. Not everyone is such a gifted swordsman.

00:38:58.460 --> 00:39:00.840
It's not a gift. No one gave it to me.

00:39:01.010 --> 00:39:02.810
I'm good because I work at it -

00:39:02.970 --> 00:39:05.730
every day of my life since I could hold a stick.

00:39:06.180 --> 00:39:09.850
I could work at fighting all day, every day, I'd still never be as good as you.

00:39:10.020 --> 00:39:12.440
Yes, well, I guess we'll never know.

00:39:22.450 --> 00:39:24.910
- Everywhere? - Everywhere.

00:39:25.070 --> 00:39:27.280
So how did it end up?

00:39:27.450 --> 00:39:32.450
- The Targaryen girl will die? - It needs to be done, unpleasant as it is.

00:39:32.620 --> 00:39:34.580
Robert's rather tasteless about it.

00:39:34.750 --> 00:39:38.210
Every time he talks about killing her, I swear the table rises six inches.

00:39:38.380 --> 00:39:41.180
It's a shame he can't muster the same enthusiasm for his wife.

00:39:41.340 --> 00:39:43.670
He does have a deep, abiding lust for her money.

00:39:43.840 --> 00:39:46.170
You have to give it to the Lannisters - they may be

00:39:46.350 --> 00:39:49.560
the most pompous, ponderous cunts the gods ever suffered to walk the world,

00:39:49.720 --> 00:39:52.350
but they do have outrageous amounts of money.

00:39:53.690 --> 00:39:57.610
- I have an outrageous amount of money. - Not as much as the Lannisters.

00:39:57.770 --> 00:40:01.150
But a lot more than you.

00:40:01.780 --> 00:40:04.530
Robert's threatening to take me hunting with him.

00:40:04.700 --> 00:40:06.660
Last time we were out there for two weeks.

00:40:06.820 --> 00:40:09.200
Tramping through the trees in the rain, day after day,

00:40:09.370 --> 00:40:12.380
all so he can stick his spear into something's flesh.

00:40:12.540 --> 00:40:15.840
But Robert loves his killing.

00:40:16.000 --> 00:40:17.880
And he's the king.

00:40:18.040 --> 00:40:21.500
- How did that ever happen? - Because he loves his killing.

00:40:21.670 --> 00:40:23.710
And he used to be good at it.

00:40:24.720 --> 00:40:27.060
Do you know who should be king?

00:40:27.510 --> 00:40:29.380
- Be serious. - I am.

00:40:29.560 --> 00:40:31.690
My father could be your bank.

00:40:31.850 --> 00:40:33.730
I've never fought in a war before,

00:40:33.890 --> 00:40:36.560
- but I'd fight for you. - I'm fourth in line.

00:40:36.730 --> 00:40:39.690
And where's Robert in the line of royal succession?

00:40:39.860 --> 00:40:42.070
Joffrey is a monster. Tommen is eight.

00:40:42.230 --> 00:40:44.730
- Stannis? - Stannis has the personality of a lobster.

00:40:44.900 --> 00:40:46.980
He's still my older brother.

00:40:47.410 --> 00:40:49.500
- What are you doing?! - Look at it.

00:40:49.660 --> 00:40:51.750
- You cut me. - It's just blood. We've all got it in us.

00:40:51.910 --> 00:40:54.200
Sometimes a little spills.

00:40:54.790 --> 00:40:57.460
If you become king, you're going to see a lot of this.

00:40:57.620 --> 00:40:59.750
You need to get used to it.

00:40:59.920 --> 00:41:01.930
Go on. Look.

00:41:03.920 --> 00:41:06.040
People love you.

00:41:07.260 --> 00:41:09.560
They love to serve you because you're kind to them.

00:41:10.140 --> 00:41:12.140
They want to be near you.

00:41:14.350 --> 00:41:17.190
You're willing to do what needs to be done,

00:41:18.230 --> 00:41:20.440
but you don't gloat over it.

00:41:20.610 --> 00:41:22.360
You don't love killing.

00:41:25.030 --> 00:41:30.120
Where is it written that power is the sole province of the worst?

00:41:30.950 --> 00:41:35.000
That thrones are only made for the hated and the feared?

00:41:38.420 --> 00:41:40.550
You would be a wonderful king.

00:41:58.350 --> 00:42:03.350
I'm sorry your marriage to Ned Stark didn't work out. You seemed so good together.

00:42:03.520 --> 00:42:06.810
I'm glad I could do something to make you happy.

00:42:10.110 --> 00:42:12.740
Without a Hand, everything will fall to pieces.

00:42:12.910 --> 00:42:17.540
I suppose this is where you tell me to give the job to your brother Jaime.

00:42:17.700 --> 00:42:19.080
No.

00:42:19.250 --> 00:42:21.260
He's not serious enough.

00:42:22.330 --> 00:42:25.330
I'll say this for Ned Stark - he's serious enough.

00:42:26.670 --> 00:42:30.210
Was it really worth it? Losing him this way?

00:42:30.380 --> 00:42:32.210
I don't know.

00:42:34.810 --> 00:42:36.480
But I do know this -

00:42:37.470 --> 00:42:42.680
if the Targaryen girl convinces her horselord husband to invade

00:42:42.860 --> 00:42:46.110
and the Dothraki horde crosses the Narrow Sea...

00:42:48.280 --> 00:42:49.870
we won't be able to stop them.
